1
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:06,817
Water, earth,

2
00:00:06,901 --> 00:00:10,195
fire, air...

3
00:00:11,322 --> 00:00:15,367
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

4
00:00:15,451 --> 00:00:18,745
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

5
00:00:19,789 --> 00:00:23,709
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

6
00:00:23,793 --> 00:00:25,627
But when the world needed him most,

7
00:00:25,712 --> 00:00:27,004
he vanished.

8
00:00:27,422 --> 00:00:31,216
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

9
00:00:31,301 --> 00:00:32,884
an airbender named Aang.

10
00:00:32,969 --> 00:00:35,262
And although his
airbending skills are great,

11
00:00:35,346 --> 00:00:38,015
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

12
00:00:38,975 --> 00:00:42,269
But I believe Aang can save the world.

13
00:01:14,552 --> 00:01:16,678
Nice try, Pupil Sangok.

14
00:01:16,763 --> 00:01:18,013
A couple of more years,

15
00:01:18,097 --> 00:01:20,349
and you might be ready
to fight a sea sponge.

16
00:01:22,518 --> 00:01:23,894
Whoa!

17
00:01:24,395 --> 00:01:27,314
Would anyone care for
a rematch with Katara?

18
00:01:29,650 --> 00:01:31,943
Katara, you've
advanced more quickly

19
00:01:32,028 --> 00:01:34,029
than any student I've ever trained.

20
00:01:34,113 --> 00:01:36,948
You have proven
that with fierce determination,

21
00:01:37,033 --> 00:01:38,784
passion, and hard work,

22
00:01:38,868 --> 00:01:40,994
you can accomplish anything.

23
00:01:41,537 --> 00:01:44,164
Raw talent alone is not enough.

24
00:01:44,248 --> 00:01:45,374
Pupil Aang!

25
00:01:45,458 --> 00:01:46,666
Yes, Master Pakku?

26
00:01:46,751 --> 00:01:49,336
Care to step into
the sparring circle?

27
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:52,214
I figure since you've found time
to play with house pets,

28
00:01:52,298 --> 00:01:55,175
you must have
already mastered waterbending.

29
00:01:55,259 --> 00:01:56,802
I wouldn't say mastered,

30
00:01:56,886 --> 00:01:58,261
but check this out!

31
00:02:08,648 --> 00:02:10,982
So, they don't have palaces
in the Southern Tribe?

32
00:02:11,067 --> 00:02:12,234
Are you kidding?

33
00:02:12,318 --> 00:02:13,693
I grew up in a block of ice.

34
00:02:13,778 --> 00:02:15,737
It's not exactly a cultural hub.

35
00:02:18,825 --> 00:02:20,867
Sokka, this is wrong.

36
00:02:20,952 --> 00:02:22,035
What's wrong?

37
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,495
We're taking a walk!

38
00:02:23,579 --> 00:02:24,830
I'm engaged.

39
00:02:24,914 --> 00:02:26,957
It just feels...

40
00:02:27,834 --> 00:02:29,167
I know what you need.

41
00:02:29,252 --> 00:02:30,877
You need to meet my good friend Appa.

42
00:02:30,962 --> 00:02:32,295
Who?

43
00:02:33,506 --> 00:02:35,632
Appa and I go way back,
don't we, boy?

44
00:02:35,716 --> 00:02:37,801
Aagh! Easy!

45
00:02:37,885 --> 00:02:38,927
Down, boy!

46
00:02:39,011 --> 00:02:40,053
No, up!

47
00:02:40,138 --> 00:02:43,014
Looks like you haven't been
giving Appa enough attention.

48
00:02:45,810 --> 00:02:47,352
So, how does this work?

49
00:02:47,437 --> 00:02:48,895
You hanging on tight?

50
00:02:50,314 --> 00:02:51,815
Yip, yip.

51
00:02:52,817 --> 00:02:55,026
My goodness!

52
00:02:56,863 --> 00:02:57,904
Wow!

53
00:02:57,989 --> 00:03:00,824
I can't believe you do this every day.

54
00:03:00,908 --> 00:03:03,285
Yeah, we pretty much live up here.

55
00:03:03,369 --> 00:03:06,079
Is it always this cold in the sky?

56
00:03:07,081 --> 00:03:08,707
Not when you're with someone.

57
00:03:10,251 --> 00:03:11,877
It's beautiful up here.

58
00:03:11,961 --> 00:03:13,003
Yeah.

59
00:03:17,508 --> 00:03:18,925
Whoo, yeah!

60
00:03:20,428 --> 00:03:22,137
Good times, good times.

61
00:03:23,514 --> 00:03:24,598
Hey, look.

62
00:03:25,558 --> 00:03:26,808
What's happening?

63
00:03:28,019 --> 00:03:29,227
No.

64
00:03:53,336 --> 00:03:54,920
- Soot.
- What?

65
00:03:55,004 --> 00:03:56,505
I've seen it before.

66
00:03:56,589 --> 00:03:58,423
Right before my village was attacked.

67
00:03:58,508 --> 00:04:00,425
It's soot mixed with snow.

68
00:04:00,510 --> 00:04:01,593
But why?

69
00:04:01,677 --> 00:04:03,345
It's the Fire Nation.

70
00:04:03,429 --> 00:04:05,222
They've closed in on the North Pole.

71
00:04:05,306 --> 00:04:06,973
And from the looks of this stuff,

72
00:04:07,058 --> 00:04:09,059
I'd say there's a lot of them.

73
00:04:12,730 --> 00:04:16,483
This will truly be one for
the history books, General Iroh.

74
00:04:16,567 --> 00:04:19,110
Just think. Centuries from now,

75
00:04:19,195 --> 00:04:21,321
people will study
the Great Admiral Zhao,

76
00:04:21,405 --> 00:04:22,656
who destroyed the last

77
00:04:22,740 --> 00:04:24,908
of the Water Tribe civilization.

78
00:04:25,243 --> 00:04:27,118
You're lucky you're here to see it.

79
00:04:27,203 --> 00:04:30,038
Be careful what you wish for, Admiral.

80
00:04:30,122 --> 00:04:33,291
History is not always kind
to its subjects.

81
00:04:33,376 --> 00:04:36,169
I suppose you speak from experience.

82
00:04:36,254 --> 00:04:39,172
But, rest assured,
this will be nothing like

83
00:04:39,257 --> 00:04:42,676
your legendary failure at Ba Sing Se.

84
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:45,095
I hope not, for your sake.

85
00:04:45,179 --> 00:04:48,306
Tell the captains to prepare
for first strike.

86
00:04:56,232 --> 00:04:58,024
We'll be landing soon.

87
00:04:58,109 --> 00:04:59,609
Do you have a plan?

88
00:04:59,694 --> 00:05:01,152
I'm working on it, Uncle.

89
00:05:11,706 --> 00:05:13,456
What's wrong? We have to go!

90
00:05:13,541 --> 00:05:14,583
No, Sokka.

91
00:05:14,667 --> 00:05:15,709
Wait.

92
00:05:15,793 --> 00:05:17,335
I can't see you anymore.

93
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:18,461
Not at all.

94
00:05:18,546 --> 00:05:20,338
What? We're just friends.

95
00:05:20,423 --> 00:05:22,632
I wish we could just be friends.

96
00:05:22,717 --> 00:05:24,217
But I like you too much,

97
00:05:24,302 --> 00:05:26,636
and it's too confusing
to be around you.

98
00:05:26,721 --> 00:05:28,763
I'm marrying someone else.

99
00:05:28,973 --> 00:05:31,349
You don't love him, do you?

100
00:05:31,434 --> 00:05:33,268
You don't even seem to like him.

101
00:05:33,352 --> 00:05:35,020
But I do love my people.

102
00:05:35,104 --> 00:05:37,439
You're not marrying them!

103
00:05:37,523 --> 00:05:39,274
You don't understand.

104
00:05:39,358 --> 00:05:40,942
I have duties to my father,

105
00:05:41,027 --> 00:05:42,235
to my tribe.

106
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:43,737
I have to do this.

107
00:05:43,821 --> 00:05:45,113
Good-bye.

108
00:05:48,117 --> 00:05:51,494
The day we have feared
for so long has arrived.

109
00:05:51,579 --> 00:05:54,581
The Fire Nation is on our doorstep.

110
00:05:54,665 --> 00:05:57,208
It is with great sadness

111
00:05:57,293 --> 00:06:00,003
I call my family here before me,

112
00:06:00,087 --> 00:06:03,214
knowing well that some of these faces

113
00:06:03,299 --> 00:06:06,301
are about to vanish from our tribe.

114
00:06:07,261 --> 00:06:10,764
But they will never vanish
from our hearts.

115
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:14,851
Now, as we approach
the battle for our existence,

116
00:06:14,935 --> 00:06:18,063
I call upon the great spirits.

117
00:06:19,315 --> 00:06:21,149
Spirit of the ocean,

118
00:06:21,233 --> 00:06:24,944
spirit of the moon, be with us!

119
00:06:25,029 --> 00:06:29,074
I'm going to need volunteers
for a dangerous mission.

120
00:06:29,492 --> 00:06:31,534
-Count me in.
-Sokka...

121
00:06:31,619 --> 00:06:32,994
Be warned.

122
00:06:33,079 --> 00:06:35,747
Many of you will not return.

123
00:06:35,831 --> 00:06:37,749
Come forward to receive my mark

124
00:06:37,833 --> 00:06:40,335
if you accept the task.

125
00:07:07,321 --> 00:07:10,156
The stillness before battle
is unbearable.

126
00:07:10,241 --> 00:07:12,742
Such a quiet dread.

127
00:07:12,827 --> 00:07:15,745
I wasn't there when the Fire Nation
attacked my people.

128
00:07:16,414 --> 00:07:18,540
I'm gonna make a difference this time.

129
00:08:04,545 --> 00:08:05,628
Yip, yip!

130
00:08:10,593 --> 00:08:11,843
Katara!

131
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:36,075
I'll take it from here, boy.

132
00:09:46,063 --> 00:09:47,272
Appa!

133
00:09:50,818 --> 00:09:52,277
Thanks for the rescue, buddy.

134
00:10:13,966 --> 00:10:15,800
You've gotta be kidding me.

135
00:10:18,387 --> 00:10:21,890
Men, you'll be infiltrating
the Fire Nation navy.

136
00:10:22,224 --> 00:10:26,185
That means you'll all need
one of these uniforms.

137
00:10:31,692 --> 00:10:33,234
What's your problem?

138
00:10:33,319 --> 00:10:35,778
Fire navy uniforms
don't look like that.

139
00:10:35,863 --> 00:10:37,488
Of course they do.

140
00:10:37,573 --> 00:10:41,075
These are real uniforms captured
from actual fire navy soldiers.

141
00:10:41,368 --> 00:10:43,620
When, like, 100 years ago?

142
00:10:44,079 --> 00:10:45,455
85.

143
00:10:45,539 --> 00:10:47,874
The Fire Nation doesn't wear
shoulder spikes anymore.

144
00:10:47,958 --> 00:10:51,044
The newer uniforms
are more streamlined.

145
00:10:51,128 --> 00:10:52,962
How do we know we can trust this guy?

146
00:10:53,047 --> 00:10:55,548
Such bold talk for a new recruit.

147
00:10:55,633 --> 00:10:57,759
Sokka is from our sister tribe, Hahn.

148
00:10:57,843 --> 00:11:02,096
He is a capable warrior,
and I value his input.

149
00:11:02,431 --> 00:11:05,224
Now, our first objective
is to determine

150
00:11:05,309 --> 00:11:08,144
the identity
of their commanding officer.

151
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,938
His name is Zhao.

152
00:11:10,856 --> 00:11:13,608
Middle-aged, big sideburns,
bigger temper...

153
00:11:13,984 --> 00:11:17,737
Sokka, I want you to tell
everything you know to Hahn.

154
00:11:17,821 --> 00:11:19,614
He's leading this mission.

155
00:11:19,698 --> 00:11:21,908
Hahn, show Sokka your respect.

156
00:11:21,992 --> 00:11:25,703
I expect nothing less
from my future son-in-law.

157
00:11:28,165 --> 00:11:29,916
Princess Yue's marrying you?

158
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:31,584
Yeah. What of it?

159
00:11:31,669 --> 00:11:33,795
Nothing. Congratulations.

160
00:11:40,427 --> 00:11:42,178
Stop those fireballs!

161
00:11:51,563 --> 00:11:53,481
It's almost twilight, Admiral.

162
00:11:53,565 --> 00:11:54,857
As your military consultant,

163
00:11:54,942 --> 00:11:57,694
I must advise you to halt your attack.

164
00:11:57,778 --> 00:12:00,780
The waterbenders draw their power
from the moon,

165
00:12:00,864 --> 00:12:02,949
and it is nearly full tonight.

166
00:12:03,033 --> 00:12:06,160
You should wait
and resume the attack at daybreak.

167
00:12:06,245 --> 00:12:08,246
I am well aware
of the moon problem.

168
00:12:08,330 --> 00:12:11,124
And I'm working on a solution.

169
00:12:11,208 --> 00:12:13,793
But for now, daybreak it is.

170
00:12:20,843 --> 00:12:22,468
They've stopped firing.

171
00:12:22,553 --> 00:12:23,594
Aang!

172
00:12:29,810 --> 00:12:32,895
I can't do it.

173
00:12:32,980 --> 00:12:34,313
What happened?

174
00:12:34,398 --> 00:12:36,774
I must have taken out
a dozen fire navy ships,

175
00:12:36,859 --> 00:12:39,569
but there's just too many of them.

176
00:12:39,653 --> 00:12:41,195
I can't fight them all!

177
00:12:41,280 --> 00:12:43,072
But you have to.

178
00:12:43,157 --> 00:12:44,574
You're the Avatar.

179
00:12:44,658 --> 00:12:46,659
I'm just one kid.

180
00:12:56,462 --> 00:12:58,755
If you are fishing
for an octopus, my nephew,

181
00:12:58,839 --> 00:13:01,257
you need a tightly woven net,

182
00:13:01,341 --> 00:13:05,053
or he will squeeze through
the tiniest hole and escape.

183
00:13:05,137 --> 00:13:07,138
I don't need your wisdom
right now, Uncle.

184
00:13:07,222 --> 00:13:10,641
I'm sorry, I just nag you because...

185
00:13:10,726 --> 00:13:14,062
Well, ever since I lost my son...

186
00:13:14,521 --> 00:13:16,939
Uncle, you don't have to say it.

187
00:13:17,024 --> 00:13:19,484
I think of you as my own.

188
00:13:21,695 --> 00:13:23,112
I know, Uncle.

189
00:13:23,197 --> 00:13:24,363
We'll meet again.

190
00:13:26,158 --> 00:13:27,992
After I have the Avatar.

191
00:13:30,996 --> 00:13:33,122
Remember your breath of fire.

192
00:13:33,207 --> 00:13:34,791
It could save your life out there.

193
00:13:34,875 --> 00:13:35,917
I will.

194
00:13:36,001 --> 00:13:37,835
And put your hood up.

195
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:39,629
Keep your ears warm.

196
00:13:39,713 --> 00:13:41,005
I'll be fine!

197
00:13:49,515 --> 00:13:50,932
Let me tell you, Sokka,

198
00:13:51,016 --> 00:13:54,185
I've courted a lot of girls,
but Yue is the finest.

199
00:13:54,269 --> 00:13:56,270
And she comes with the most perks.

200
00:13:56,355 --> 00:13:58,606
Perks?! What does that mean?

201
00:13:58,690 --> 00:14:00,983
I mean,
Yue's nice and everything,

202
00:14:01,068 --> 00:14:03,152
but the points I'll gain
with the chief aren't bad either.

203
00:14:03,237 --> 00:14:06,864
Princess Yue is wasted
on a self-absorbed weasel like you!

204
00:14:07,241 --> 00:14:08,574
Whoa, hang on!

205
00:14:08,659 --> 00:14:09,826
What do you care?

206
00:14:09,910 --> 00:14:12,328
You're just a simple rube
from the Southern Tribe.

207
00:14:12,412 --> 00:14:15,414
What would you know of the political
complexities of our life?

208
00:14:15,499 --> 00:14:16,707
No offense.

209
00:14:20,504 --> 00:14:23,256
You're just a jerk without a soul!
No offense!

210
00:14:25,843 --> 00:14:27,176
That's enough!

211
00:14:27,261 --> 00:14:29,929
Sokka, you're off the mission.

212
00:14:30,556 --> 00:14:32,306
All right, fall in, men!

213
00:14:32,391 --> 00:14:34,183
Everybody listen to what I say,

214
00:14:34,268 --> 00:14:37,270
and we'll take out this Admiral Cho
in no time!

215
00:14:37,354 --> 00:14:39,147
It's Admiral Zhao!

216
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:16,767
Where are they going?

217
00:15:18,687 --> 00:15:20,855
They're coming up for air somewhere.

218
00:15:30,032 --> 00:15:33,117
The legends say the moon
was the first waterbender.

219
00:15:33,202 --> 00:15:35,786
Our ancestors saw how it pushed
and pulled the tides,

220
00:15:35,871 --> 00:15:37,788
and learned how to do it themselves.

221
00:15:37,873 --> 00:15:41,292
I've always noticed
my waterbending is stronger at night.

222
00:15:41,376 --> 00:15:44,253
Our strength comes from
the spirit of the moon,

223
00:15:44,338 --> 00:15:46,714
our life comes from the spirit
of the ocean.

224
00:15:46,798 --> 00:15:49,383
They work together to keep balance.

225
00:15:49,593 --> 00:15:50,843
The spirits.

226
00:15:50,928 --> 00:15:53,679
Maybe I can find them
and get their help.

227
00:15:53,764 --> 00:15:55,139
How can you do that?

228
00:15:55,224 --> 00:15:56,766
The avatar is the bridge

229
00:15:56,850 --> 00:15:58,851
between our world
and the spirit world.

230
00:15:58,936 --> 00:16:00,311
Aang can talk to them!

231
00:16:00,395 --> 00:16:03,356
Maybe they'll give you the wisdom
to win this battle.

232
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:04,899
Or maybe they'll unleash

233
00:16:05,025 --> 00:16:07,485
a crazy-amazing spirit attack
on the Fire Nation!

234
00:16:09,529 --> 00:16:11,197
Or wisdom. That's good, too.

235
00:16:11,281 --> 00:16:12,990
The only problem is,

236
00:16:13,075 --> 00:16:15,493
the last time you got
to the spirit world by accident.

237
00:16:15,577 --> 00:16:17,286
How are you going
to get there this time?

238
00:16:17,371 --> 00:16:19,622
I have an idea. Follow me.

239
00:16:26,505 --> 00:16:28,464
So, is this the way
to the spirit world?

240
00:16:28,548 --> 00:16:29,632
Ha ha ha. No.

241
00:16:29,716 --> 00:16:32,593
You'll have to get there on your own.
But I can take you

242
00:16:32,678 --> 00:16:35,846
to the most spiritual place
in the entire North Pole.

243
00:16:52,698 --> 00:16:55,616
I never thought
I'd miss grass this much!

244
00:16:55,701 --> 00:16:58,494
It's so warm here!
How is that possible?

245
00:16:58,578 --> 00:17:01,872
It's the center
of all spiritual energy in our land.

246
00:17:11,300 --> 00:17:12,800
You're right, Yue.

247
00:17:12,884 --> 00:17:14,468
I can feel...

248
00:17:14,553 --> 00:17:15,636
Something.

249
00:17:15,721 --> 00:17:16,929
It's so...

250
00:17:17,014 --> 00:17:18,431
Tranquil.

251
00:17:36,283 --> 00:17:37,325
Be quiet!

252
00:17:57,512 --> 00:17:59,513
Is something wrong, Sokka?

253
00:17:59,598 --> 00:18:00,723
No.

254
00:18:00,807 --> 00:18:02,391
Hahn's out there
on the top-secret mission,

255
00:18:02,476 --> 00:18:04,352
while I'm here
sharpening my boomerang.

256
00:18:04,436 --> 00:18:05,728
Everything's fine.

257
00:18:05,812 --> 00:18:07,271
Listen to me.

258
00:18:07,356 --> 00:18:10,066
I took you off the mission
for selfish reasons.

259
00:18:10,150 --> 00:18:13,152
I have a special task in mind for you.

260
00:18:13,236 --> 00:18:14,945
What, you want me
to scrub the barracks?

261
00:18:15,030 --> 00:18:18,908
I want you to guard my daughter,
Princess Yue.

262
00:18:19,451 --> 00:18:21,327
Sure.

263
00:18:21,411 --> 00:18:23,204
That shouldn't be too hard.

264
00:19:16,216 --> 00:19:18,175
Why is he sitting like that?

265
00:19:18,260 --> 00:19:19,552
He's meditating.

266
00:19:19,636 --> 00:19:21,846
Trying to cross over
into the spirit world.

267
00:19:22,139 --> 00:19:24,098
It takes all his concentration.

268
00:19:24,516 --> 00:19:26,225
Is there any way we can help?

269
00:19:26,309 --> 00:19:27,977
How about some quiet?!

270
00:19:28,061 --> 00:19:31,188
Come on, guys,
I can hear every word you're saying.

271
00:19:51,710 --> 00:19:52,793
Is he ok?

272
00:19:52,878 --> 00:19:54,670
He's crossing into the spirit world.

273
00:19:54,754 --> 00:19:57,131
He'll be fine as long as
we don't move his body.

274
00:19:57,215 --> 00:19:59,550
That's his way back
to the physical world.

275
00:19:59,634 --> 00:20:00,968
Maybe we should get some help?

276
00:20:01,052 --> 00:20:02,595
No. He's my friend.

277
00:20:02,679 --> 00:20:04,972
I'm perfectly capable
of protecting him.

278
00:20:05,348 --> 00:20:08,267
Well, aren't you a big girl now?

279
00:20:08,351 --> 00:20:09,393
No...

280
00:20:09,478 --> 00:20:10,519
Yes.

281
00:20:10,604 --> 00:20:13,063
Hand him over
and I won't have to hurt you.

282
00:20:15,817 --> 00:20:16,984
Hyah!

283
00:20:24,951 --> 00:20:26,619
I see you've learned a new trick.

284
00:20:26,703 --> 00:20:28,579
But I didn't come this far
to lose to you.

285
00:20:48,808 --> 00:20:50,893
You little peasant.

286
00:20:50,977 --> 00:20:53,020
You've found a master, haven't you?

287
00:20:56,566 --> 00:20:58,025
Hyah!

288
00:21:03,114 --> 00:21:04,532
Hyah! Hyah...

289
00:21:09,329 --> 00:21:11,330
Aah! Uh!

290
00:21:12,082 --> 00:21:13,916
Hyah! Hyah...

291
00:21:27,097 --> 00:21:29,348
It's daybreak at last.

292
00:21:29,724 --> 00:21:31,725
Let's write history.

293
00:21:53,582 --> 00:21:57,418
You rise with the moon,
I rise with the sun.

294
00:22:08,888 --> 00:22:12,516
The Water Tribe can try
to resist the inevitable,

295
00:22:13,310 --> 00:22:15,853
but their city will fall today.

296
00:22:23,236 --> 00:22:25,029
Aang?!

297
00:22:26,906 --> 00:22:28,824
What happened?! Where's Zuko?!

298
00:22:28,908 --> 00:22:30,034
He took Aang.

299
00:22:30,118 --> 00:22:32,453
He took him right out from under me.

300
00:22:33,121 --> 00:22:34,913
Where did they go?
